    "lawCode": "Amd §§100, 152 & 153, Ec Dev L (as proposed in S.9268 & A.10036)",
    "lawSection": "Economic Development Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S798\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN S\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the economic development law, in relation to the\npromotion of local small businesses listed on the registry of historic\nbusinesses\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nChapter Amendment. To require the Department of Economic Development to\npromote small businesses listed on the registry of historic businesses\nmaintained by the Department of Parks, Recreation, and Historic Preser-\nvation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nChapter Amendment.\n\nSection 1: Includes the requirement of promoting small businesses listed\non the registry of historic businesses to the rights and duties of the\nDepartment of Economic Development.\n\nSection 2: Requires the Department of Economic Development to report on\nthe effectiveness of the efforts to support historic small businesses\nthrough the \"I Love NY\" brand-based promotions.\n\nEffective thirty days after it shall become law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe majority of businesses in New York State are small businesses, many\nof which reflect and enhance the rich history and traditions of their\nlocal communities. New York's registry of historic businesses celebrates\nunique and iconic business that have operated in New York communities\nfor 50 years or longer (with no more than a two-year break) and provides\na ready-resource of historic tourist attractions.  This bill capitalizes\non the durability, success, and ingenuity of New York's historic small\nbusinesses by celebrating them through the state's long-standing \"I Love\nNY\" campaign. By directing ESD to include Historic Small Business\npromotion in its marketing guidance and grant eligibility, the state\nwill help ensure the survival of these long-standing businesses in the\nfuture.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024:\n\nS.9268 (Ryan) - Passed Senate on 5/30/24, 57-0.\n\nA.10036(Woerner)- Passed Assembly on 5/30/24, 144-0.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the Economic Development Law in\nrelation to the promotion of local small businesses listed on the regis-\ntry of historic businesses.\n",
